{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-0c340524-cf87-4fc4-8e95-49d48a783613","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-b697e5ab4a1ab2c5","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8008-n6x5i9hx/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-8008-E002.md","content":"# KEDA TriggerAuthentication reconciler for LLMInferenceService in odh-model-controller\n\n## Description\n\nThis epic delivers the downstream KEDA TriggerAuthentication flow in odh-model-controller so that LLMInferenceService standalone KEDA Prometheus-type triggers can query Thanos/Prometheus with an authenticated context on OpenShift. On OpenShift, KEDA ScaledObjects cannot query Thanos/Prometheus without authentication; this epic creates the per-namespace authentication resources for LLMInferenceService standalone KEDA, mirroring the flow that already exists for v1beta1 InferenceService KEDA autoscaling.\n\n## Scope\n\n- A parallel reconciler flow in odh-model-controller for LLMInferenceService standalone KEDA with Prometheus-type triggers, following the existing `kserve_keda_reconciler` pattern at `internal/controller/serving/reconcilers/kserve_keda_reconciler.go`.\n- Per-namespace authentication resources, matching the existing reference implementation's resource set: a dedicated ServiceAccount (`inference-prometheus-auth`), a ServiceAccountToken Secret (`kubernetes.io/service-account-token` type), a Role/RoleBinding for metrics access, and a KEDA TriggerAuthentication CR supplying bearer token and CA cert to KEDA's Prometheus triggers.\n- Owner reference management and lifecycle cleanup consistent with the existing reconciler (resources garbage-collected with the owning LLMInferenceService).\n- Reuse of the existing reconciler's conventions for resource naming so operators see a consistent authentication surface across v1beta1 InferenceService and LLMInferenceService.\n- Identification and implementation of any OpenShift-specific RBAC or TLS adjustments this flow requires beyond the existing v1beta1 pattern (the strategy's open question on downstream adaptation is resolved here for the authentication context; TLS 1.2+ via the TriggerAuthentication CR per the security NFR).\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- Given an LLMInferenceService with the standalone KEDA spec configured with Prometheus-type triggers, when the odh-model-controller reconciles, then the per-namespace authentication resources are created: ServiceAccount, ServiceAccountToken Secret, Role/RoleBinding, and KEDA TriggerAuthentication CR, measured by `kubectl get` returning each resource in the target namespace.\n- Given an LLMInferenceService using the KEDA TriggerAuthentication flow, when KEDA evaluates a Prometheus trigger, then the query succeeds with ServiceAccount token authentication over TLS 1.2+, measured by the ScaledObject reporting the trigger as active and no authentication errors in KEDA operator logs.\n- Given an LLMInferenceService is deleted, when the reconciler performs lifecycle cleanup, then the owned authentication resources are removed, measured by owner-reference garbage collection leaving no orphans.\n- LLMInferenceService CRs without standalone KEDA Prometheus triggers produce no authentication resources, measured by no TriggerAuthentication CRs in namespaces without qualifying CRs.\n- Existing v1beta1 InferenceService KEDA authentication behavior is unchanged, measured by the existing `kserve_keda_reconciler` integration tests passing unmodified.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-1 (P0): LLMInferenceService supports standalone KEDA autoscaling with user-defined triggers without requiring WVA deployment — this epic supplies the OpenShift authentication context that makes the primary supported trigger source (Prometheus/Thanos queries) functional.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":40435,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9cbc04831ea090fb","agent_id":"a7506effac068fb42","session_id":"975609a4-9996-4dcf-a42c-1d087396c61b","uuid":"43a25747-e133-4e5b-a1a2-75c40af7b795","timestamp":"2026-10-22T06:30:40.964Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8008"}
