{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9fe79a756b91898a","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8008\n3\tepic_count: 3\n4\tcritical_path_length: 3\n5\tdecompose_complete: true\n6\trevised: false\n7\ttriage: null\n8\ttriage_rationale: null\n9\t---\n10\t# Decomposition Summary: RHAISTRAT-8008\n11\t\n12\tInference-Aware Autoscaling for llm-d — standalone KEDA primitives for LLMInferenceService.\n13\t\n14\tStaff Engineer / SME Input section is empty (template placeholder only) — no overrides to apply.\n15\t\n16\t## Epic List\n17\t\n18\t| ID | Title | Type | Team | Priority |\n19\t|----|-------|------|------|----------|\n20\t| RHAISTRAT-8008-E001 | Standalone KEDA autoscaling path for LLMInferenceService in kserve llmisvc-controller | Implementation | Serving team | P0 |\n21\t| RHAISTRAT-8008-E002 | KEDA TriggerAuthentication reconciler for LLMInferenceService in odh-model-controller | Implementation | Serving team | P0 |\n22\t| RHAISTRAT-8008-E003 | Autoscaling decision guide and configuration documentation for LLMInferenceService | Implementation (docs-authoring) | Documentation team | P0 |\n23\t\n24\t## Dependency DAG\n25\t\n26\t```mermaid\n27\tgraph TD\n28\t    E001[RHAISTRAT-8008-E001 Standalone KEDA path in llmisvc-controller]\n29\t    E002[RHAISTRAT-8008-E002 TriggerAuthentication reconciler in odh-model-controller]\n30\t    E003[RHAISTRAT-8008-E003 Autoscaling documentation]\n31\t    E001 --> E002\n32\t    E001 --> E003\n33\t    E002 --> E003\n34\t```\n35\t\n36\tCritical path: E001 → E002 → E003 (length 3).\n37\t\n38\t## DAG Justification\n39\t\n40\t| Edge | Rule | Rationale |\n41\t|------|------|-----------|\n42\t| E001 → E002 | Rule 13 (build-against artifact) | E001 lands the standalone KEDA spec in the LLMInferenceService v1alpha2 API (ScalingSpec `keda` field, CEL validation). The odh-model-controller reconciler's code builds against those API types and reconciles CRs carrying the new fields — a build-against API/CRD artifact, not a configuration reference. |\n43\t| E001 → E003 | Rule 11 (docs last) | Documentation describes the implemented API and behavior; blocked by every Implementation epic. |\n44\t| E002 → E003 | Rule 11 (docs last) | Documentation must cover the OpenShift TriggerAuthentication flow delivered by the odh-model-controller work. |\n45\t\n46\tNotes on edges deliberately NOT drawn:\n47\t\n48\t- No Investigation epics were created (see Unknowns Analysis below). All three strategy open questions fail the \"does the answer change which downstream epics exist or what they do\" test — they change content or in-epic scope, not epic structure.\n49\t- Upstream PR kserve/kserve#5839 is modeled as a precondition with a defined fallback (carry the patch downstream), per Rule 21 third-party-resolves case — an acceptance criterion on E001, not a separate upstream epic.\n50\t- No konflux-onboarding / repo-onboarding / license-validation epics: kserve and odh-model-controller are existing platform components with architecture context files; the change extends existing code in already-onboarded repos.\n51\t\n52\t## HLR Traceability Matrix\n53\t\n54\t| HLR | Priority | Epic(s) |\n55\t|-----|----------|---------|\n56\t| HLR-1: Standalone KEDA autoscaling with user-defined triggers without WVA | P0 | E001, E002 |\n57\t| HLR-2: Mutual exclusivity of WVA and standalone KEDA paths (CEL validation) | P0 | E001 |\n58\t| HLR-3: Scale-to-zero via KEDA `idleReplicaCount: 0` (both paths) | P0 | E001 |\n59\t| HLR-4: Scale-from-zero (standalone KEDA via user-configured triggers) | P0 | E001 |\n60\t| HLR-5: Independent prefill/decode scaling in disaggregated deployments | P0 | E001 |\n61\t| HLR-6: Scaling events with signal attribution | P1 | E001 |\n62\t| HLR-7: Decision-guide documentation covering both paths | P1 | E003 |\n63\t\n64\tFull coverage: every HLR maps to at least one epic; no orphaned requirements.\n65\t\n66\tHLR-6 note: the WVA-path half of this HLR