{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a3c896eca1863d7c","type":"tool_result","content":"16:**Detailed**: odh-model-controller runs as two Deployments within the RHOAI platform. The primary `odh-model-controller` Deployment is a controller-runtime operator that reconciles KServe InferenceService, InferenceGraph, LLMInferenceService, ServingRuntime, and NIM Account custom resources. It manages subordinate Kubernetes resources including Routes, NetworkPolicies, ServiceAccounts, ClusterRoleBindings, KEDA TriggerAuthentications, Kuadrant AuthPolicies, Istio EnvoyFilters, and Prometheus monitoring resources. Eight admission webhooks (5 mutating, 3 validating) intercept creation and update of inference workloads and NIM accounts. The secondary `model-serving-api` Deployment provides an HTTPS REST API for gateway discovery (`/api/v1/gateways`) and sample LLM-d templates (`/api/v1/samples/llm-d`), backed by a Kubernetes client that queries Gateway API resources. Both workloads resolve their TLS configuration from the OpenShift APIServer TLS profile, falling back to Mozilla Intermediate defaults (TLS 1.2+) on non-OpenShift clusters. The controller watches the OpenShift `config.openshift.io/v1/APIServer` resource and restarts on TLS profile changes. [source: cmd/main.go:89-177, server/main.go:27-134, server/server.go:16-44, pkg/tls/tls.go:76-139]\n22:**Controller architecture.** The operator runs 10 reconcilers spanning core Kubernetes resources (ConfigMap, Secret, Pod), KServe serving resources (InferenceService, InferenceGraph, ServingRuntime), LLM-specific resources (LLMInferenceService, Gateway), NIM account management, and OpenShift APIServer TLS profile watching. The InferenceServiceReconciler is the most broadly connected, owning subordinate watches on 13 resource types including Routes, NetworkPolicies, ServiceAccounts, ClusterRoleBindings, PodMonitors, ServiceMonitors, ServingRuntimes, and KEDA TriggerAuthentications. The GatewayReconciler manages Gateway API resources, Kuadrant AuthPolicies, Istio EnvoyFilters, and PodMonitors for the LLM gateway ingress path. A conditional prometheus-operator watch allows the controller to degrade gracefully when monitoring CRDs are absent. [source: cmd/main.go:89-177, internal/controller/serving/inferenceservice_controller.go:208-219, internal/controller/serving/llm/gateway_controller.go:1003-1062]\n28:**Platform integration pattern.** The controller reads `DataScienceCluster` and `DSCInitialization` CRs to determine which platform components are enabled, gating feature-specific behavior. It manages Kuadrant AuthPolicies for LLMInferenceService authentication, creates KEDA TriggerAuthentications for autoscaling, and provisions OpenShift Routes for model serving endpoints. The SelfSubjectAccessReview call in the gateway discoverer validates the caller's permissions before exposing gateway information. [source: config/rbac/role.yaml:3, server/gateway/discovery.go:154-171]\n213:| odh-model-controller-role | keda.sh | triggerauthentications | create, delete, get, list, patch, update, watch |\n338:The InferenceServiceReconciler watches InferenceService, ServingRuntime, ConfigMap, Secret, and Namespace resources. On reconciliation, it creates or updates subordinate resources including Services, ServiceAccounts, NetworkPolicies, ClusterRoleBindings, Routes, PodMonitors, ServiceMonitors, and KEDA TriggerAuthentications. [source: internal/controller/serving/inferenceservice_controller.go:208-219, config/rbac/role.yaml:3]\n419:| keda.sh/v1alpha1/TriggerAuthentication | Controller watch (Owns) |  |  | Kubernetes API | TLS | InferenceServiceReconciler |\n---kserve---\n22:**Controller topology.** The `manager` binary reconciles the foundational CRDs — InferenceService, InferenceGraph, ClusterServingRuntime, and TrainedModel — creating Deployments, Services, and ingress resources (HTTPRoutes, Istio VirtualServices, or OpenShift Routes depending on platform configuration). The `llmisvc` controller handles the LLMInferenceService and LLMInferenceServiceConfig CRDs with extensive Gateway API integration, managing HorizontalPodAutoscalers, LeaderWorkerSets for multi-node inference, KEDA ScaledObjects, and InferencePool resources for gateway-based load balancing. The `localmodel`/`localmodelnode` pair manages persistent model caching at cluster and node level through PersistentVolume/PersistentVolumeClaim lifecycle and batch Job-based model downloads. The `kserve-module` operator runs from a separate Go module (`kserve-module/`) and manages the installation and configuration of all other KServe components on the ODH/RHOAI platform, watching the `Kserve` CR from `components.platform.opendatahub.io`. [source: pkg/controller/v1beta1/inferenceservice/controller.go:724, pkg/controller/v1alpha2/llmisvc/controller.go:419, pkg/controller/v1alpha1/localmodel/reconcilers/localmodelcache_reconciler.go:365, kserve-module/pkg/kservemodule/setup.go:68]\n220:| github.com/kedacore/keda/v2 | v2.18.0 | Yes |  | Go module dependency |\n434:| kserve-manager-role | keda.sh | scaledobjects, scaledobjects/finalizers | create, delete, get, list, patch, update, watch |\n435:| kserve-manager-role | keda.sh | scaledobjects/status | get, patch, update |\n465:| kserve-llmisvc-manager-role | keda.sh | scaledobjects | create, delete, get, list, patch, update, watch |\n633:- **Controller reconciliation:** Each controller watches its primary CRDs and creates/updates owned Kubernetes resources. The InferenceService controller creates Deployments, Services, and ingress resources (HTTPRoutes, Ingresses, VirtualServices, or Routes). The LLMISVC controller extends this with HPA, KEDA ScaledObjects, LeaderWorkerSets, InferencePools, and Gateway resources. The local model controllers manage PersistentVolumes, PersistentVolumeClaims, and batch Jobs for node-level model downloads. All controllers communicate with the Kubernetes API via in-cluster ServiceAccount tokens over TLS. [source: pkg/controller/v1beta1/inferenceservice/controller.go:669, pkg/controller/v1alpha2/llmisvc/controller.go:419, pkg/controller/v1alpha1/localmodel/reconcilers/localmodelcache_reconciler.go:340]\n724:| keda.sh/v1alpha1/ScaledObject | Controller watch (Owns) |  |  | Kubernetes API | TLS | InferenceServiceReconciler |\n725:| keda.sh/v1alpha1/ScaledObject | Controller watch (Owns) |  |  | Kubernetes API | TLS | LLMISVCReconciler |","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-ad0da4a90b4435dd","agent_id":"af4153aabb1820807","session_id":"975609a4-9996-4dcf-a42c-1d087396c61b","uuid":"2c255912-3425-4990-9018-4026dadcc3fc","timestamp":"2026-10-22T06:34:57.298Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-a3c896eca1863d7c","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-8008 decomposition"}
