 epics. Captured as acceptance criteria on E001 (scale-to-zero and metric-outage ACs from the strategy).\n91\t\n92\t## Health Warnings\n93\t\n94\t- **Pending process gates**: Architecture Review, Build Onboarding, Licence Validation, and other Prerequisites are all \"Pending human review\" — the strategy is in Refinement. Decomposition assumes sign-off; a materially different review outcome would require re-decomposition.\n95\t- **Upstream timing risk**: E001 depends on kserve/kserve#5839 (open, assigned). Fallback (carry the patch downstream with backport) is an explicit AC on E001; if the PR is rejected rather than delayed, E001's approach needs rework — monitor upstream.\n96\t- **External inputs to documentation**: E003 content depends on inputs the Documentation team does not control (scale-from-zero SLO from the llm-d team; Prometheus capacity guidance from Performance/PSAP). If unavailable, E003 ships with the RFE-referenced 60-second p50 and a capacity-tuning section marked as guidance pending PSAP validation.\n97\t- **Docs priority**: E003 is P0 solely via the docs-authoring priority rule (strategy frontmatter `priority: Critical` → P0); its underlying HLR is P1. Not a priority inversion — rule-driven — but planners should treat it as P1-value work sequenced last.\n98\t- **HLR-6 split ownership**: the WVA-events half of the observability HLR is owned by RHAISTRAT-7670; only the standalone-KEDA half is covered here. Action: confirm RHAISTRAT-7670's scope explicitly covers WVA scaling-event visibility before treating HLR-6 as closed across strategies.\n99\t\n100\t## Tiered Delivery\n101\t\n102\tEvaluated per Step 5.5 for the uncertain-timing external dependency (kserve/kserve#5839):\n103\t\n104\t- Partial value without upstream landing is limited to carrying the patch downstream — which delivers the full capability, not a tier. The odh-model-controller work (E002) builds against the API delivered by E001 and cannot ship user value ahead of it; documentation (E003) describes the built surface.\n105\t- **Conclusion: no Tier 1 / Tier 2 split.** The fallback (carry patch downstream) is recorded as an acceptance criterion on E001, matching the strategy's stated mitigation. If upstream lands on time, E001 simply consumes the rebase instead.\n106\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9c5dcd31d50731d0","agent_id":"afbfd982328e0cbff","session_id":"975609a4-9996-4dcf-a42c-1d087396c61b","uuid":"c8c3f0e6-bd8c-4b33-8747-b7fa719bb737","timestamp":"2026-10-22T06:40:01.481Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-b540ac061597dd53","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-8008"}
